      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=-18)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "We construct an interval around $X=-18$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14225558/assets/9ccbf2335f4db52e60760d4740ebf29ac054b6b249b6f0436e02fbff3311d7d4.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=-18) & ≈P(-18-0.5\\le Y\\le -18+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-18.5\\le Y\\le -17.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
